WEBVTT

1
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:32.450
a Sony Company

2
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.525
Hi. My name is Peter Parker.

3
00:01:16.766 --> 00:01:19.291
You don't remember me.
but I have something to tell you...

4
00:01:19.726 --> 00:01:21.576
that's gonna sound crazy.

5
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.011
But it's the truth.

6
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.496
And I know you're gonna believe me...

7
00:01:29.576 --> 00:01:32.450
because you're very good at telling when I'm lying.

8
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.700
E.V.. can you check the calibration of my targeting matrix?

9
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.525
That doesn't feel zeroed in to me.

10
00:01:38.692 --> 00:01:40.750
Checking target calibration.

11
00:01:49.527 --> 00:01:50.961
Hey. E.V.. take five.

12
00:01:51.481 --> 00:01:52.580
Standing by.

13
00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.603
We used to know each other.

14
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.747
We were together.

15
00:02:04.075 --> 00:02:05.736
But something bad was gonna happen...

16
00:02:05.761 --> 00:02:09.457
and the only way to stop it was to make everyone forget me.

17
00:02:14.139 --> 00:02:16.454
First day at MIT. let's go!

18
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.775
My gosh! We're here! We made it!

19
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.175
MJ. come on.

20
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.563
Including you.

21
00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:23.210
Pretend like you're not the happiest you've ever been...

22
00:02:23.323 --> 00:02:24.623
in your entire life right now.

23
00:02:25.706 --> 00:02:26.575
I can't.

24
00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.200
-Let's just do this! You're happy!
-Okay. okay. okay. Okay.

25
00:02:29.586 --> 00:02:31.585
Because I'm not just Peter Parker.

26
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.600
I'm Spider-Man.

27
00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:38.209
I'm really. really understanding the culture out here in Boston is just so different.

28
00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.984
And sometimes Spider-Man has to do the hard thing...

29
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.925
even if it breaks Peter Parker's heart.

30
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.400
And everyone here is like.
"Pahk the cah by the hahba.

31
00:02:47.722 --> 00:02:49.825
And maybe that's my responsibility.

32
00:02:50.665 --> 00:02:52.225
To live alone with the truth.

33
00:02:53.678 --> 00:02:57.425
But the truth is. MJ. that I love you.

34
00:02:58.900 --> 00:02:59.845
And I hope that deep down...

35
00:02:59.985 --> 00:03:02.425
something inside of you remembers that you love me. too.

36
00:03:03.886 --> 00:03:06.400
Suspect is 5'8". 5'10". medium build.

37
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.625
But until then. I'm just gonna be Spider-Man.

38
00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:16.602
Incoming!

39
00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:20.959
Hey. get him!

40
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.769
Hey. hey. hey. Whoa. whoa. whoa!

41
00:03:36.811 --> 00:03:38.518
Members of the Manfredi crime syndicate...

42
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.191
were apprehended by Spider-Man yesterday.

43
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.750
Hey. we live on the same floor.

44
00:04:04.852 --> 00:04:05.785
Cool.

45
00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.960
Does anybody ever come up here?

46
00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.550
Not unless they like asbestos.

47
00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.750
We've just been using it for storage.

48
00:04:17.997 --> 00:04:19.200
It's perfect.

49
00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.200
Hey. everyone. sophomore-year-Ned is back.

50
00:04:23.626 --> 00:04:26.200
Older. wiser. flyer.

51
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.600
Let's go!

52
00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.950
-What is on your face?
-How do you feel about it?

53
00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.850
I mean. you look like an assistant coach.

54
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.425
You sure you wanna do this. Scorpion?

55
00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.100
Did you miss me. Spidey?

56
00:04:48.365 --> 00:04:49.458
If I drop you from here...

57
00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.725
how long you think
it will take you to hit the ground?

58
00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.450
Well. I don't know. You tell me.

59
00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.919
Let's end this on a high note?

60
00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.373
Yo. Lonnie!

61
00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:05.934
Wha ha happened?

62
00:05:06.266 --> 00:05:09.616
DeWolff. all the evidence you're gonna need is in the trunk of his car.

63
00:05:10.039 --> 00:05:11.925
You tryin' to take my job. Spider-Man?

64
00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.438
Hey. you guys are the professionals.
I'm just a volunteer.

65
00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.850
It's a new New York.

66
00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:30.425
Thanks to Spider-Man.
crime rates have dropped to a record low.

67
00:05:30.798 --> 00:05:32.850
Police and Damage Control give much of the credit...

68
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.050
to the masked hero.

69
00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.225
Initiate HUD test.

70
00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.250
Armed robbery at Civic Union Bank.

71
00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:39.600
In the past six months.
he has taken down...

72
00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.400
every major crime lord across the five boroughs...

73
00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.425
including the superpowered ninja group The Hand.

74
00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.060
A Worker Survives Near-Fatal Oil Rig Emergency

75
00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.400
He is the pride of New York City.

76
00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:55.925
The hero every grown-up relies on and every kid wants to be.

77
00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.380
Final semester. MIT.

78
00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:02.057
My gosh. we're graduating in a month.

79
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.650
We've made so many memories.
Where do I begin?

80
00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.750
Night swimming in the Charles River with Jim and Wiley.

81
00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.650
The infamous food fun at the Banana Lounge.

82
00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:16.050
Pulling all-nighters in Stud 5 with MJ and Nate Dawg.

83
00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.750
It feels like yesterday
I was sitting on a roof with MJ...

84
00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.025
dreaming about coming here together.
and I still can't believe we did it.

85
00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.825
I'm so grateful for all the friends that I've made.

86
00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.225
I couldn't imagine going through this with anyone else.

87
00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.525
Ned. who do you think is actually watching these?

88
00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.086
-I don't know. But maybe someone.
-Okay.

89
00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.605
Okay. well. bye. someone.

90
00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.727
-What? No!
-Bye. We're done. Yeah. we're done.

91
00:06:46.443 --> 00:06:48.463
Lasciare davanti alla porta

92
00:06:53.376 --> 00:06:56.376
-Parliamo del centro di Brooklyn
-in pieno giorno.

93
00:06:56.605 --> 00:06:59.078
Un colpo cosi. lo sai che c'entra Foswell.

94
00:06:59.111 --> 00:06:59.804
High profile job like that.
you know that Foswell was involved.

95
00:06:59.829 --> 00:07:01.779
Yeah. I hear you. but can you prove it?

96
00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.550
Yeah. I'm going through his financial records...

97
00:07:03.971 --> 00:07:05.358
and I'm following his crew every night.

98
00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.250
Do you do anything besides work?

99
00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:09.825
You know the saying.
"You do something you love...

100
00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.292
you don't work a day in your life.

101
00:07:12.846 --> 00:07:14.696
-Mom. where's my calculator?
-I don't know.

102
00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:18.450
Trust me. aight?
Being married to the job never ends well.

103
00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.650
Well. don't worry about it. I'll be okay.

104
00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.550
Yeah?
You still getting them headaches. though?

105
00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.425
Yeah. But I'll be fine.

106
00:07:27.611 --> 00:07:28.550
I don't know. man.

107
00:07:28.853 --> 00:07:30.778
I think you're body's tryin' to tell you somethin'.

108
00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:33.325
Like you need to get outta that suit every once in a while.

109
00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.425
Mom. do you know where my calculator is?

110
00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:36.564
I don't know. Papi.

111
00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.725
What you need is some real human connection.

112
00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:41.450
What? And we're not connecting?

113
00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:46.250
Nah. dude. I don't know your name.
your face. or nothing about you.

114
00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.600
I don't think you've ever asked me a question about my life.

115
00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:49.825
Sure. I have.

116
00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.232
Yeah. what are my kids' names?

117
00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.687
Well. for starters. your son's name's Papi.

118
00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:56.600
Is it Spider-Man?

119
00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.710
I can't tell you that. sweetheart.

120
00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:00.550
That means it's Spider-Man.

121
00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:01.825
Gosh.

122
00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:07.050
A hijacked tank is heading southbound past 34th Street.

123
00:08:07.427 --> 00:08:08.713
All available units respond.

124
00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.125
Hey. you getting this?

125
00:08:10.375 --> 00:08:11.901
More work. Lucky you.

126
00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.283
Okay. I'll see you out there.

127
00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:14.703
I'm so sorry. I gotta go.

128
00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:32.950
I got you. Spidey!

129
00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.625
No. no. I don't need your...

130
00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:49.812
Hey! Heads up!

131
00:09:51.837 --> 00:09:54.810
You okay. kid? Yeah. you're okay.
See ya later.

132
00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:00.625
You wouldn't know it just by looking at it...

133
00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.000
but this very street was completely destroyed in the Battle of New York.

134
00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.225
Come on. come on. come on.

135
00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.450
Come on.

136
00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:31.450
God.

137
00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.294
Come on.

138
00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:42.807
Hey.

139
00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.150
The hell. Frank?
You just hit me with the van!

140
00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:47.533
Quit your whimpering.

141
00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:49.050
We're not doing that again. Frank.

142
00:10:49.328 --> 00:10:50.576
You're goddamn right we're not.

143
00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.600
This time you're gonna get the hell outta my way.

144
00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:54.644
You mean. instead of saving your life?

145
00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.850
You gonna talk about that Staten Island bullshit again?

146
00:10:58.232 --> 00:10:59.425
Well. you said it. not me.

147
00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:00.378
Jeez.

148
00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.625
Look. man. you can't just shoot yourself out of every situation.

149
00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:03.975
Innocent people get hurt.

150
00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.625
Who do you think's downrange of that tank. dumb-dumb?

151
00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:13.225
Suit yourself.

152
00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:17.850
Jackass.

153
00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:19.850
This freakin' guy.

154
00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.175
Go home. Frank!

155
00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:43.450
I'm gonna kill this kid.

156
00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.250
-DeWolff?
-Are you gonna stop that thing or what?

157
00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:53.050
It's heading straight for the Damage Control Detention Center.

158
00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.250
I'm trying.

159
00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:55.050
Try harder.

160
00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.050
There's a lot of scary dudes locked up in there.

161
00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.625
Well. who do you think put them in there?

162
00:11:59.839 --> 00:12:02.989
Let's go. Scorpion. Moving day.

163
00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:35.960
All right. everybody. clear out!
This guy is armed and dangerous.

164
00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.870
Get out of the vehicle. ma'am.

165
00:12:50.446 --> 00:12:52.451
I was thinking the same thing.

166
00:13:01.045 --> 00:13:02.339
Spider-Man?

167
00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:05.025
Where am I?

168
00:13:12.206 --> 00:13:13.166
What?

169
00:13:15.823 --> 00:13:17.103
Move! Move! Move!

170
00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.016
Keep her for questioning.
Clear the building.

171
00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:24.150
Enjoy the ride. Scorpion!

172
00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.950
You won't be seeing much daylight in supermax.

173
00:13:27.893 --> 00:13:29.700
Scorpions are nocturnal. buddy.

174
00:13:33.105 --> 00:13:36.116
The building is under attack.
Get the prisoner out of here now!

175
00:13:41.494 --> 00:13:42.574
Sir!

176
00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.700
You gotta take off now!

177
00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.725
The building has been breached. Go! Go!

178
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:07.950
Hey. fire it up! Go! Go!

179
00:14:16.239 --> 00:14:17.352
Change of plans!

180
00:14:18.019 --> 00:14:19.945
Take him to the helipad at Bellevue.

181
00:14:20.676 --> 00:14:23.950
-What?
-That's an order from Director Metzger. Go!

182
00:14:24.013 --> 00:14:25.038
Now!

183
00:14:25.108 --> 00:14:26.155
Copy that.

184
00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.725
Hey! What...

185
00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:40.350
How did I get up here?

186
00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:47.428
Spider-Man. save me. would you?

187
00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.264
Who are you?

188
00:14:55.453 --> 00:14:56.657
You can see me.

189
00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.443
Tell me who you are.

190
00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:00.817
You first.

191
00:15:03.666 --> 00:15:06.247
Hey. Hey.

192
00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:13.050
You pushed me out.

193
00:15:13.699 --> 00:15:14.805
Interesting.

194
00:15:14.978 --> 00:15:16.225
What the hell was that?

195
00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.725
Did you just try to jump into my mind?

196
00:15:18.872 --> 00:15:21.861
You know. the whole time you've been chasing me...

197
00:15:22.577 --> 00:15:25.279
you forgot to ask yourself a very important question.

198
00:15:27.054 --> 00:15:28.340
What's in the tank?

199
00:15:30.404 --> 00:15:31.857
Go! Move.

200
00:15:46.053 --> 00:15:47.280
Spider-Man?

201
00:15:48.259 --> 00:15:49.392
What just happened?

202
00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:53.542
I don't know.

203
00:15:55.674 --> 00:15:56.725
Hey. good job.

204
00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:57.721
Hey. way to go. Spidey.

205
00:15:57.841 --> 00:15:59.550
You guys okay? You good?

206
00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:02.352
I swear. All the things they said I did.
I don't remember doing any of them.

207
00:16:02.679 --> 00:16:04.750
It's okay. it's okay.
Look. let these people take good care of you.

208
00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:05.874
I would never hurt you.

209
00:16:05.939 --> 00:16:07.147
-Okay.
-I love you. Spider-Man.

210
00:16:07.495 --> 00:16:08.809
Yeah. All right. buddy. All right.

211
00:16:08.975 --> 00:16:11.065
-Hey. what do you got?
-Here. get this.

212
00:16:11.125 --> 00:16:12.750
Chopper took Scorpion to Bellevue.

213
00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.150
Ten minutes later.
a guard walked him right out the door.

214
00:16:15.206 --> 00:16:16.331
What?

215
00:16:16.673 --> 00:16:17.620
What about the tank?

216
00:16:17.812 --> 00:16:20.249
Stolen from the Damage Control warehouse in Brooklyn.

217
00:16:20.493 --> 00:16:22.593
Driver was a janitor who worked there.

218
00:16:22.879 --> 00:16:23.753
You got a motive?

219
00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:24.726
Nada.

220
00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:25.977
And no criminal record.

221
00:16:26.047 --> 00:16:28.103
Scorpion must've gotten to her somehow.

222
00:16:29.153 --> 00:16:30.725
Yeah. Maybe.

223
00:16:30.967 --> 00:16:32.329
What do you mean. "maybe"?

224
00:16:32.575 --> 00:16:34.362
I mean. I don't know.

225
00:16:35.373 --> 00:16:36.592
But I know someone that might.

226
00:16:36.758 --> 00:16:37.832
Where you going?

227
00:16:37.913 --> 00:16:39.413
You keep following the leads on Scorpion.

228
00:16:39.601 --> 00:16:41.151
I'm gonna go talk to someone.

229
00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:00.250
Hi. is this 3250 Brighton Beach?

230
00:17:04.977 --> 00:17:05.925
Okay.

231
00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:08.350
I think I know what that means.

232
00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:14.895
Take off your clothes.

233
00:17:17.855 --> 00:17:18.925
What?

234
00:17:19.327 --> 00:17:21.407
You don't wear clothes in the banya.

235
00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:23.782
Ditch the leotard.

236
00:17:24.946 --> 00:17:26.250
This is not a leotard.

237
00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.165
Your text said that this was your office.

238
00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:31.925
This is my office.

239
00:17:32.748 --> 00:17:33.628
Get in.

240
00:17:34.961 --> 00:17:36.376
I'm fine. thanks. I'll just...

241
00:17:37.691 --> 00:17:39.091
My office. my rules.

242
00:17:39.266 --> 00:17:42.849
This way you get to enjoy a nice. relaxing soak...

243
00:17:43.153 --> 00:17:45.229
and I get to see that
you don't have any weapons...

244
00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:46.669
and we both win.

245
00:17:48.763 --> 00:17:49.800
Okay.

246
00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.431
Really? What. you never take that off?

247
00:18:01.731 --> 00:18:03.850
No. I... You know. it defeats the whole anonymous thing.

248
00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:08.300
Even for your girlfriend or boyfriend or whatever?

249
00:18:09.086 --> 00:18:10.812
There's a lot of conjecture online.

250
00:18:11.486 --> 00:18:13.950
And super graphic artwork. Have you seen?

251
00:18:14.282 --> 00:18:16.750
The one with you and the ten Mysterios. it's...

252
00:18:17.132 --> 00:18:19.100
I've seen it. I've...

253
00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:20.650
It's hard to unsee. to be honest.

254
00:18:20.945 --> 00:18:22.925
But. look. I don't have anyone.
I just kinda keep to myself.

255
00:18:23.757 --> 00:18:25.331
All by yourself? All the time?

256
00:18:25.557 --> 00:18:26.964
No wonder you're so sad.

257
00:18:27.137 --> 00:18:29.056
-I'm not so sad.
-A little bit.

258
00:18:29.233 --> 00:18:31.083
Could we just talk about what I came here to talk to you about...

259
00:18:31.335 --> 00:18:32.741
the attack on Damage Control?

260
00:18:32.848 --> 00:18:36.625
Yes. So. that is more your area.

261
00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:39.687
