The results of your body scan show a surge in the hormones...

523
00:37:26.562 --> 00:37:28.825
associated with your arachnid DNA...

524
00:37:28.900 --> 00:37:31.625
...resulting in the formation of organic web spinnerettes...

525
00:37:31.844 --> 00:37:34.650
and dangerously heightened sensory receptors.

526
00:37:34.900 --> 00:37:37.125
Okay. but I feel fine.

527
00:37:37.180 --> 00:37:41.442
Prolonged isolation or emotional trauma could be contributing to this sudden change.

528
00:37:41.700 --> 00:37:45.002
Have you experienced any recent traumatic events?

529
00:37:47.913 --> 00:37:48.999
Peter?

530
00:37:49.572 --> 00:37:50.921
I'm fine. E.V..

531
00:37:50.946 --> 00:37:52.224
You don't seem fine.

532
00:37:52.304 --> 00:37:54.817
I recommend you take some time to rebalance.

533
00:37:54.977 --> 00:37:57.054
Well. that's not really an option. is it?

534
00:38:13.300 --> 00:38:15.669
Mechanical web shooters and organic webs

535
00:38:15.733 --> 00:38:17.637
cannot be used simultaneously.

536
00:38:19.376 --> 00:38:22.100
Come on. Peter.

537
00:38:40.500 --> 00:38:42.995
Alert. Senses are overloaded.

538
00:38:45.195 --> 00:38:47.440
Alert. Senses are overloaded.

539
00:38:49.810 --> 00:38:52.756
Alert. Senses are overloaded.

540
00:38:56.550 --> 00:38:58.237
What the hell was that?

541
00:38:58.660 --> 00:39:02.505
Your heightened senses are taking in too much information at once.

542
00:39:03.305 --> 00:39:07.126
Okay. It's okay.

543
00:39:07.151 --> 00:39:09.662
All right. organic webs. Peter Two had 'em.

544
00:39:09.776 --> 00:39:11.625
He was cool. You're cool.

545
00:39:20.408 --> 00:39:21.775
My God. that's hideous.

546
00:39:22.787 --> 00:39:23.947
Okay. here we go.

547
00:39:25.911 --> 00:39:27.197
Okay. that didn't work.

548
00:39:28.645 --> 00:39:30.825
Organic webs. Come on! And bam!

549
00:39:34.500 --> 00:39:35.650
No. no!

550
00:39:38.565 --> 00:39:39.650
Stop!

551
00:39:43.467 --> 00:39:44.685
What's going on. E.V.?

552
00:39:44.772 --> 00:39:48.194
Shots fired at the Damage Control Data Center in Manhattan.

553
00:39:48.307 --> 00:39:50.750
Suspect facial match with Scorpion.

554
00:39:51.075 --> 00:39:52.400
Okay. I'm on my way.

555
00:39:52.810 --> 00:39:54.592
Come on. Three. two...

556
00:39:54.980 --> 00:39:56.035
Web! Stop!

557
00:39:59.309 --> 00:40:00.822
Web! Stop!

558
00:40:02.290 --> 00:40:03.250
Stop!

559
00:40:03.576 --> 00:40:05.571
Web! Stop! Birds. birds. birds!

560
00:40:06.500 --> 00:40:07.477
Web! Stop.

561
00:40:11.700 --> 00:40:13.225
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

562
00:40:13.885 --> 00:40:15.105
Web! Stop.

563
00:40:15.459 --> 00:40:16.450
God!

564
00:40:17.100 --> 00:40:18.625
Web! Stop. stop. stop.

565
00:40:43.100 --> 00:40:45.025
I don't know what you're looking for.

566
00:40:45.214 --> 00:40:47.014
I'm looking for V-Max.

567
00:40:49.639 --> 00:40:51.700
I don't know anything.

568
00:40:51.900 --> 00:40:53.279
I'll see for myself.

569
00:40:56.595 --> 00:40:57.595
God. God!

570
00:41:06.135 --> 00:41:08.648
I'm sorry I'm late.
I've had a really crazy day.

571
00:41:27.355 --> 00:41:30.822
Scorpion. do we really gotta keep doing this? My head is killing me.

572
00:41:31.734 --> 00:41:33.280
You think I'm Scorpion?

573
00:41:35.117 --> 00:41:35.991
Web!

574
00:41:37.899 --> 00:41:39.172
What's happening to you?

575
00:41:47.319 --> 00:41:48.751
You can't sense me anymore.

576
00:41:52.479 --> 00:41:53.396
You.

577
00:41:53.586 --> 00:41:55.350
What's going on with you. Spider-Man?

578
00:42:04.739 --> 00:42:07.339
Warning. Arachnid hormones increasing.

579
00:42:22.700 --> 00:42:23.938
Who are you?

580
00:42:24.700 --> 00:42:26.312
Do you know who you are?

581
00:42:50.300 --> 00:42:52.468
-We need some help over here.
-Yes. coming through.

582
00:43:01.500 --> 00:43:02.605
Spider-Man.

583
00:43:05.187 --> 00:43:06.275
What the hell?

584
00:43:06.532 --> 00:43:08.026
Somebody get a medic.

585
00:43:28.300 --> 00:43:29.657
DeWolff. is she hurt?

586
00:43:30.554 --> 00:43:31.667
Is she okay?

587
00:43:31.993 --> 00:43:33.187
-Is she okay?
-No!

588
00:43:33.254 --> 00:43:35.508
-Just let me go...
-Don't! What is going on with you?

589
00:43:35.562 --> 00:43:36.795
That wasn't Scorpion. okay.

590
00:43:36.886 --> 00:43:40.562
I mean it was. but he was possessed by whatever hijacked that tank. okay.

591
00:43:40.780 --> 00:43:42.815
-Look. please can I just...
-All right. listen. Slow down.

592
00:43:45.500 --> 00:43:49.169
Listen. I don't know what this is.
but I need you to pull it together.

593
00:43:49.782 --> 00:43:51.236
You almost killed a cop.

594
00:43:54.035 --> 00:43:55.425
This isn't you.

595
00:43:55.770 --> 00:43:56.963
I know. I'm sorry.

596
00:43:57.350 --> 00:43:59.898
If you act like this again.
I cannot protect you.

597
00:44:00.960 --> 00:44:03.518
Whatever this is. you need to fix it.

598
00:44:24.952 --> 00:44:27.212
Through lattice chromodynamics...

599
00:44:28.612 --> 00:44:32.225
we can arrange time and space in a grid.

600
00:44:32.366 --> 00:44:37.532
Which allows us to simulate the quarks binding into the protons.

601
00:44:38.300 --> 00:44:42.252
Cindy. is this a question about protons or more stuff about Avengers?

602
00:44:43.500 --> 00:44:46.238
Okay. Guys. I love to tell stories...

603
00:44:46.384 --> 00:44:49.446
but you know I gotta teach you some physics at some point here.

604
00:44:53.722 --> 00:44:55.850
All right. Let it rip. Cindy.

605
00:44:56.060 --> 00:44:59.060
Well. if Thanos was so worried about over-population...

606
00:44:59.205 --> 00:45:02.069
why didn't he just use the magic glove to make more food?

607
00:45:06.300 --> 00:45:08.702
Arthur. you wanna answer that question?

608
00:45:09.464 --> 00:45:12.600
Hulk smash!

609
00:45:16.346 --> 00:45:17.871
There you have it.

610
00:45:19.100 --> 00:45:21.237
Excuse me. Dr. Banner. I...

611
00:45:23.500 --> 00:45:25.550
-You okay?
-Yeah. sorry. it's just a headache.

612
00:45:25.850 --> 00:45:28.250
Have you got a minute?
I wanted to talk to you about your inhibitor.

613
00:45:29.946 --> 00:45:32.799
Sure. Don't worry. It's got failsafes.

614
00:45:33.100 --> 00:45:37.172
I'm not gonna turn into the big green raging monster machine in the cafeteria.

615
00:45:37.845 --> 00:45:40.279
But if you do see me with this thing off. run.

616
00:45:43.840 --> 00:45:47.025
No. but. you're using target-specific short interfering RNA. right?

617
00:45:48.666 --> 00:45:51.861
It's like gene silencing. you're just incorporating the gamma radiation?

618
00:45:54.188 --> 00:45:55.722
What'd you say your name was?

619
00:45:56.928 --> 00:45:59.394
Ned... Leeds.

620
00:45:59.900 --> 00:46:02.697
So you found a way to suppress the expression of DNA...

621
00:46:03.037 --> 00:46:05.892
even as it's undergoing the mutation due to gamma radiation. right?

622
00:46:06.165 --> 00:46:08.412
-Yes.
-Okay. so. my question is...

623
00:46:09.430 --> 00:46:14.427
would that same thing be possible with DNA that's mutating for another reason?

624
00:46:16.388 --> 00:46:17.595
What's the reason?

625
00:46:19.268 --> 00:46:20.512
I don't know.

626
00:46:21.409 --> 00:46:25.091
Let's say that the host genome is mixed with some kind of foreign DNA.

627
00:46:25.546 --> 00:46:26.696
Theoretically.

628
00:46:27.500 --> 00:46:30.370
Theoretically? Yes. that's possible. Yes.

629
00:46:31.125 --> 00:46:34.275
So. could you suppress only some parts of that DNA expression?

630
00:46:34.433 --> 00:46:37.083
Like the bad aspects but just keep all of the good stuff?

631
00:46:37.975 --> 00:46:41.250
You mean. like. if I wanted to keep some parts of Hulk but not others?

632
00:46:41.397 --> 00:46:42.480
Right.

633
00:46:42.620 --> 00:46:46.792
It would be enormously dangerous and complex. but...

634
00:46:47.900 --> 00:46:51.847
if you were able to target the correct mRNA strand...

635
00:46:52.615 --> 00:46:53.455
Possibly.

636
00:46:53.748 --> 00:46:56.015
Wait. so you could just turn the mutating gene on and off...

637
00:46:56.300 --> 00:46:58.745
as long as you do it before the mRNA transcription?

638
00:46:59.398 --> 00:47:00.271
Maybe.

639
00:47:02.650 --> 00:47:05.023
I mean. if you apply the same thinking.
you could even...

640
00:47:05.599 --> 00:47:07.616
develop some kind of automatic inhibitor...

641
00:47:07.742 --> 00:47:10.564
that would just adjust to any type of mutation.

642
00:47:11.779 --> 00:47:14.550
Well. now you're talking about a universal inhibitor...

643
00:47:14.678 --> 00:47:17.800
that would control anyone who has any powers.

644
00:47:19.186 --> 00:47:20.472
It's a dangerous idea.

645
00:47:21.633 --> 00:47:23.725
Well. yeah. But it's theoretical. right?

646
00:47:26.300 --> 00:47:28.076
You're not one of my students. are ya?

647
00:47:30.300 --> 00:47:32.233
No. I'm a grad student.

648
00:47:32.700 --> 00:47:33.679
I've...

649
00:47:34.826 --> 00:47:38.062
I've taken enough of your time.
I gotta get some books back to the library.

650
00:47:38.439 --> 00:47:40.040
The library is that way.

651
00:47:41.738 --> 00:47:43.898
Right. Right. Duh.

652
00:47:44.026 --> 00:47:45.576
How would you decide?

653
00:47:46.566 --> 00:47:47.680
What's that?

654
00:47:48.313 --> 00:47:50.421
Well. what parts of nature are good or bad?

655
00:47:51.062 --> 00:47:52.809
What if you're trying to control the expression...

656
00:47:53.047 --> 00:47:54.966
of something that needs to be expressed?

657
00:48:00.846 --> 00:48:02.579
Good luck with your studies. Ned.

658
00:48:04.353 --> 00:48:05.676
Thank you. Professor.

659
00:48:06.573 --> 00:48:07.547
Like reptiles...

660
00:48:07.780 --> 00:48:10.050
- God.
- ...amphibians and arthropods...

661
00:48:10.300 --> 00:48:13.300
...spiders shed skin
at key points in their life cycles.

662
00:48:13.847 --> 00:48:15.360
The process is known as molting.

663
00:48:15.900 --> 00:48:18.130
Fourth inhibitor prototype complete.

664
00:48:18.300 --> 00:48:19.503
While molting is a natural...

665
00:48:19.583 --> 00:48:21.825
-part of a spider's life cycle...
-Okay. come on. Come on.

666
00:48:21.900 --> 00:48:23.850
...it can leave the spider vulnerable to threats.

667
00:48:23.900 --> 00:48:26.263
Upload inhibitor beta build seven.

668
00:48:26.393 --> 00:48:27.443
...process is initiated by hormonal changes...

669
00:48:27.900 --> 00:48:29.825
Uploaded. Would you like to run a test?

670
00:48:30.700 --> 00:48:31.577
Yeah. run it.

671
00:48:31.900 --> 00:48:32.979
...few hours to several days.

672
00:48:33.712 --> 00:48:37.212
Spiders have three stages in their life cycle.

673
00:48:37.500 --> 00:48:40.525
Each stage is characterized by physical changes...

674
00:48:40.726 --> 00:48:45.779
with the largest changes occurring during the beautiful transition to adulthood.

675
00:48:45.990 --> 00:48:47.625
A LIFE IN WEBS: Journey through the life cycle of a spider

676
00:48:48.527 --> 00:48:50.200
For those who make it through...

677
00:48:50.300 --> 00:48:52.650
molting amounts to a kind of rebirth.

678
00:48:52.700 --> 00:48:54.057
Can you turn that spider stuff off?

679
00:48:54.204 --> 00:48:55.557
Turning off video.

680
00:48:56.300 --> 00:48:57.863
-Inhibitor active.
-Okay. here we go.

681
00:48:57.973 --> 00:48:59.205
Come on. Come on.

682
00:49:00.910 --> 00:49:02.397
Keep an eye on my vitals.

683
00:49:04.878 --> 00:49:06.436
Inhibitor engaged.

684
00:49:10.490 --> 00:49:14.169
Suppressing arachnid hormones to your baseline levels.

685
00:49:17.019 --> 00:49:18.099
Okay.

686
00:49:21.840 --> 00:49:23.340
All right. E.V.. let's do this.

687
00:49:23.499 --> 00:49:25.449
Initiating field test one.

688
00:49:27.500 --> 00:49:28.405
That's working.

689
00:49:28.600 --> 00:49:31.467
Alert. Inhibitor is overheating.
Functionality reducing.

690
00:49:31.492 --> 00:49:32.575
INHIBITOR OVERHEATING

691
00:49:32.600 --> 00:49:34.125
Yeah. I'm sensing that.

692
00:49:34.273 --> 00:49:36.123
Alert. Senses are overloaded.

693
00:49:36.200 --> 00:49:39.328
Alert. Senses are overloaded.
Senses are overloaded. Alert.

694
00:49:41.046 --> 00:49:42.927
Web grenades activated.

695
00:49:43.060 --> 00:49:44.214
GRENADES ACTIVATED

696
00:49:45.140 --> 00:49:46.222
Oh sh...

697
00:49:58.473 --> 00:50:00.660
Inhibitor field test one. failure.

698
00:50:03.800 --> 00:50:06.450
Yo. Spider-Man. you okay?

699
00:50:07.219 --> 00:50:09.273
Yeah. I'm just trying out some new tech.

700
00:50:10.200 --> 00:50:12.812
Yeah. To get rid of that monster inside you?

701
00:50:18.200 --> 00:50:19.689
Still can't sense me?

702
00:50:21.246 --> 00:50:23.151
Guess your technology isn't working.

703
00:50:24.359 --> 00:50:26.867
You know. you're the only person I've met that I can't...

704
00:50:27.800 --> 00:50:29.069
hop into.

705
00:50:29.813 --> 00:50:31.713
I'm sure that's really frustrating for you.

706
00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:33.375
I'll get in there one day.

707
00:50:33.586 --> 00:50:34.737
What do you want?

708
00:50:36.327 --> 00:50:41.427
I wanna know why a half-human. half-spider would decide to work for an organization...

709
00:50:41.800 --> 00:50:45.100
whose sworn mission is to hunt down anybody who's different.

710
00:50:46.420 --> 00:50:48.926
Damage Control isn't after you because you're different.

711
00:50:49.675 --> 00:50:51.375
They're hunting you down because you're dangerous.

712
00:50:51.579 --> 00:50:53.309
Now. what do you want?

713
00:50:53.933 --> 00:50:58.078
Since you're a very simple spider.
let me spell it out for you.

714
00:50:59.000 --> 00:51:01.495
Damage Control has something that I need.

715
00:51:02.479 --> 00:51:04.063
You mean V-Max?

716
00:51:06.800 --> 00:51:10.184
I was planning to use Scorpion to get it.
but you keep getting in my way.

717
00:51:10.699 --> 00:51:13.049
I will always be in your way.

718
00:51:13.334 --> 00:51:15.975
You sure about that. Peter Parker?

719
00:51:21.000 --> 00:51:24.550
You know. your apartment is kinda like a parody...

720
00:51:24.792 --> 00:51:27.561
of where you think a sad single guy in his 20s might live.

721
00:51:27.960 --> 00:51:32.710
Take-out containers.
free weights. protein powder.

722
00:51:37.570 --> 00:51:38.910
You're bluffing.

723
00:51:39.000 --> 00:51:40.944
You know.
you're not hard to track down. Peter.

724
00:51:41.487 --> 00:51:44.745
Well. at least not for someone like me.

725
00:51:45.800 --> 00:51:47.986
I did find one interesting thing. though.

726
00:51:49.093 --> 00:51:50.560
In of all places...

727
00:51:52.600 --> 00:51:53.879
coffee cup.

728
00:51:56.373 --> 00:51:58.376
E.V.. display home work station.

729
00:52:00.600 --> 00:52:04.143
You spent four years erasing Peter Parker from existence?

730
00:52:04.956 --> 00:52:07.325
No wonder the spider's trying to swallow up the man.

731
00:52:08.164 --> 00:52:10.284
I wonder if MJ would even recognize you.

732
00:52:13.587 --> 00:52:15.080
I think I might go see how she's doing.

733
00:52:15.280 --> 00:52:16.339
I'm not gonna let that happen.

734
00:52:16.473 --> 00:52:20.336
No. her roommate was nice enough to post a new address online.

735
00:52:20.600 --> 00:52:23.422
How about this? I'll race you there.

736
00:52:23.906 --> 00:52:25.144
If you touch her...

737
00:52:25.446 --> 00:52:26.952
Better start swinging.

738
00:52:27.400 --> 00:52:28.554
I'm fast.

739
00:52:51.877 --> 00:52:52.937
Hey.

740
00:52:53.097 --> 00:52:54.990
It's a long way to MJ's.

741
00:52:56.113 --> 00:52:57.603
You better pick up the pace.

742
00:53:04.600 --> 00:53:06.550
E.V.. track physical anomalies.

743
00:53:07.731 --> 00:53:10.550
Searching for physical anomalies between subjects.

744
00:53:10.710 --> 00:53:12.017
Please stand by.

745
00:53:16.560 --> 00:53:18.966
Thank you all so much for coming today.

746
00:53:26.016 --> 00:53:27.141
I'm sorry about that.

747
00:53:27.166 --> 00:53:29.091
Give it up for Spider-Man...

748
00:53:29.373 --> 00:53:32.473
In a race for the love of his life.
and it's not looking good.

749
00:53:34.747 --> 00:53:36.953
Come on. Spidey. Keep up.

750
00:53:38.200 --> 00:53:39.248
Excuse me. Sorry.

751
00:53:47.953 --> 00:53:49.097
Spider-Man!

752
00:53:52.652 --> 00:53:54.462
E.V.. run these numbers with the others.

753
00:53:57.800 --> 00:53:59.947
Analyzing jump distances for patterns.

754
00:54:02.493 --> 00:54:04.018
Get me that jump data.

755
00:54:04.200 --> 00:54:05.370
Calculating.

756
00:54:09.380 --> 00:54:10.930
Come on. I need an answer!

757
00:54:12.286 --> 00:54:13.936
Calculations complete.

758
00:54:29.559 --> 00:54:31.688
You have a limit to your jump radius. don't ya?

759
00:54:32.313 --> 00:54:33.657
Thirty-three feet.

760
00:54:34.406 --> 00:54:36.869
I don't see anybody up here for you to hop into.

761
00:54:37.900 --> 00:54:39.088
Very clever.

762
00:54:39.587 --> 00:54:42.918
Like I said. you're not getting near her.

763
00:54:58.380 --> 00:55:00.035
-Hey. hey. hey.
-MJ! I'm sorry. but you're in danger.

764
00:55:00.135 --> 00:55:01.075
-Where's your roommate?
-What?

765
00:55:01.100 --> 00:55:02.016
Where's Ned?

766
00:55:02.200 --> 00:55:03.455
In Boston with friends. Why?

767
00:55:03.519 --> 00:55:04.680
Okay. good. You gotta come with me.

768
00:55:04.920 --> 00:55:06.150
What? I don't know if you're the real Spider-Man.

769
00:55:06.600 --> 00:55:08.013
-I'm not coming with you.
-We don't have time for this.

770
00:55:08.273 --> 00:55:10.326
-Please. Come on.
-You need to get out of my apartment.

771
00:55:10.539 --> 00:55:11.686
Look. this is gonna sound insane...

772
00:55:11.859 --> 00:55:13.984
but there is someone who is after you who is really dangerous. okay?

773
00:55:14.339 --> 00:55:16.275
And I promised you
that I would keep you safe.

774
00:55:17.400 --> 00:55:19.439
Please. you just have to trust me. Come on.

775
00:55:22.766 --> 00:55:23.937
Fine.

776
00:55:30.600 --> 00:55:31.610
Web. Stop.

777
00:55:35.282 --> 00:55:36.300
Web. Stop.

778
00:55:40.333 --> 00:55:41.432
Web stop.

779
00:55:47.000 --> 00:55:48.236
-Are you okay?
-Yeah. yeah. I'm fine.

780
00:55:48.416 --> 00:55:50.805
Okay. We should be safe up here.

781
00:55:51.000 --> 00:55:52.258
Okay. well. safe from what?

782
00:55:53.473 --> 00:55:54.788
I'm not entirely sure.

783
00:55:55.080 --> 00:55:56.717
Okay. well. what do they want with me?

784
00:55:56.810 --> 00:55:58.805
-I don't know.
-You don't know?

785
00:55:59.536 --> 00:56:02.126
It doesn't make any sense.
Why would they choose me?

786
00:56:02.399 --> 00:56:04.599
I wish I could tell you. I just...

787
00:56:07.459 --> 00:56:09.026
We knew each other. didn't we?

788
00:56:12.799 --> 00:56:13.762
What?

789
00:56:14.600 --> 00:56:16.011
It's the only explanation.

790
00:56:17.400 --> 00:56:18.663
It's been driving me crazy for years...

791
00:56:18.763 --> 00:56:21.262
all the times that Spider-Man saved either me or Ned.

792
00:56:21.879 --> 00:56:22.831
It was the Washington Monument...

793
00:56:23.000 --> 00:56:25.603
and then it was London and Prague and the Night Monkey.

794
00:56:26.506 --> 00:56:29.138
I mean. twice is a coincidence.
but over and over again...

795
00:56:31.357 --> 00:56:33.250
We knew each other. Tell me I'm wrong.

796
00:56:35.300 --> 00:56:36.175
Well. you're wrong.

797
00:56:36.200 --> 00:56:39.071
What were we?
Were we classmates or friends or something?

798
00:56:39.694 --> 00:56:41.947
Look. I don't know what you're talking about.

799
00:56:42.046 --> 00:56:43.327
Were we something more?

800
00:56:45.426 --> 00:56:47.432
I just. I can't. I can't remember.

801
00:56:47.800 --> 00:56:49.727
And I feel like someone scrambled my brain.

802
00:56:49.893 --> 00:56:51.807
And you're the only one who would know why.

803
00:56:52.600 --> 00:56:53.868
This is crazy. I can't...

804
00:56:54.255 --> 00:56:56.310
I know that you can't tell me the truth.

805
00:56:59.000 --> 00:57:00.309
But I need to know.

806
00:57:05.493 --> 00:57:07.613
Maybe there's a part of me that still remembers.

807
00:57:48.200 --> 00:57:49.197
Peter.

808
00:57:51.160 --> 00:57:52.150
MJ.

809
00:57:52.200 --> 00:57:53.287
Hey. Peter.

810
00:57:59.800 --> 00:58:01.330
I've missed you so much.

811
00:58:06.291 --> 00:58:07.951
I can't believe you figured it out.

812
00:58:08.492 --> 00:58:09.591
I did.

813
00:58:15.440 --> 00:58:17.815
Go ahead. Peter. Touch her.

814
00:58:19.173 --> 00:58:20.472
Hold her.

815
00:58:21.800 --> 00:58:23.495
You've been wanting to for so long.

816
00:58:32.052 --> 00:58:33.839
True love's kiss breaks the spell...

817
00:58:34.659 --> 00:58:36.614
and reunites the star-crossed lovers.

818
00:58:38.728 --> 00:58:40.421
MJ would vomit.

819
00:58:42.600 --> 00:58:44.429
You really are a simple spider. aren't you?

820
00:58:47.800 --> 00:58:49.052
I see why you like her.

821
00:58:49.520 --> 00:58:50.752
She's...

822
00:58:51.706 --> 00:58:53.131
she's smart...

823
00:58:53.729 --> 00:58:54.902
funny...

824
00:58:55.566 --> 00:58:56.990
and a little dark and twisted.

825
00:59:00.940 --> 00:59:02.166
I mean. it is sad.

826
00:59:03.079 --> 00:59:06.400
There is. like. no thoughts of you in here...

827
00:59:07.653 --> 00:59:09.017
whatsoever.

828
00:59:10.393 --> 00:59:11.941
But you knew that. didn't you?

829
00:59:13.113 --> 00:59:14.471
You're a monster.

830
00:59:15.400 --> 00:59:16.988
If you loved someone the way that I love her...

831
00:59:17.095 --> 00:59:19.770
then you'd know that
what you're doing right now is unforgivable.

832
00:59:19.947 --> 00:59:21.149
Is that so?

833
00:59:28.200 --> 00:59:31.433
You know. some people would kill to hold the person they love one last time.

834
00:59:33.080 --> 00:59:34.416
Stop it now.

835
00:59:44.333 --> 00:59:45.977
You're running out of time. Peter.

836
00:59:46.799 --> 00:59:50.479
Soon enough. it won't just be your friends who don't remember Peter Parker.

837
00:59:51.800 --> 00:59:53.597
Maybe you should write a letter to yourself.

838
00:59:58.146 --> 00:59:59.285
Get out of her.

839
01:00:00.712 --> 01:00:02.341
Who's the monster now. Peter?

840
01:00:25.516 --> 01:00:26.370
MJ.

841
01:00:27.000 --> 01:00:28.850
MJ. No. no. no. God.

842
01:00:29.472 --> 01:00:30.910
God. please. no. come on.

843
01:00:31.173 --> 01:00:32.370
Come on. come on. come on.

844
01:00:32.940 --> 01:00:35.402
Thank God. Thank God.

845
01:00:35.559 --> 01:00:38.284
You're okay. You're okay.

846
01:00:38.548 --> 01:00:39.895
I'm so sorry.

847
01:00:42.219 --> 01:00:44.387
Stop. Wait. wait. stop. stop.
please. I'll quit.

848
01:00:44.600 --> 01:00:46.827
You win. you win. you win.
Just don't hurt her.

849
01:00:49.800 --> 01:00:51.422
You're a mess. Spider-Man.

850
01:00:53.959 --> 01:00:55.409
Anytime I want...

851
01:00:55.533 --> 01:00:56.956
I can be anyone I want.

852
01:00:58.200 --> 01:00:59.998
So you can't protect MJ...

853
01:01:01.333 --> 01:01:02.846
even from herself.

854
01:01:10.380 --> 01:01:11.852
It really is a nice letter.

855
01:01:12.727 --> 01:01:13.880
Little heavy-handed.

856
01:01:13.946 --> 01:01:15.167
But not bad.

857
01:01:26.266 --> 01:01:27.419
SCANNING COMPLETE

858
01:01:34.027 --> 01:01:36.464
You're okay.
I'm gonna take you someplace safe.

859
01:01:36.600 --> 01:01:37.678
What?

860
01:01:39.000 --> 01:01:39.988
Take me to 3165...

861
01:01:40.250 --> 01:01:41.375
Lafayette Street.

862
01:01:41.616 --> 01:01:44.069
Navigating to Empire State University.

863
01:01:49.000 --> 01:01:50.234
Wait. wait. wait! Okay.

864
01:01:52.482 --> 01:01:53.548
-I got you. I got you.
-Are you sure?

865
01:01:53.800 --> 01:01:54.690
-Yep.
-Okay.

866
01:01:54.715 --> 01:01:55.861
Cause I feel like
I'm slipping a little bit.

867
01:01:55.952 --> 01:01:57.081
-You're not slipping.
-Okay.

868
01:01:58.893 --> 01:02:00.098
You're okay. you're okay. you're okay.

869
01:02:00.200 --> 01:02:01.724
Yeah. yeah. yeah. I'm fine. I'm fine.

870
01:02:05.400 --> 01:02:06.252
Okay.

871
01:02:06.352 --> 01:02:07.520
Can we just slow down...

872
01:02:07.584 --> 01:02:09.010
-for like two seconds. please?
-Well. we're almost there.

873
01:02:09.159 --> 01:02:11.156
Yeah. yeah. but you just told me I was mind controlled.

874
01:02:11.400 --> 01:02:12.218
Well. not technically.

875
01:02:12.336 --> 01:02:13.614
I mean. you're lucky
I believe in that stuff. okay?

876
01:02:13.833 --> 01:02:15.749
Because governments have been doing it for years. especially the French.

877
01:02:16.600 --> 01:02:17.617
-Are you okay?
-Yeah...

878
01:02:17.846 --> 01:02:20.254
Look. Sorry. I'm just trying to take you someplace safe. okay?

879
01:02:24.819 --> 01:02:25.982
I don't feel safe.

880
01:02:28.377 --> 01:02:29.291
Shit.

881
01:02:34.200 --> 01:02:35.296
- Sorry.
- Watch out!

882
01:02:45.006 --> 01:02:46.302
You're losing it. kid.

883
01:02:46.600 --> 01:02:48.977
Thought you'd be able to see that coming a mile away.

884
01:02:49.057 --> 01:02:50.216
What is wrong with you?

885
01:02:50.339 --> 01:02:51.709
-You could've killed us.
-Excuse me.

886
01:02:52.066 --> 01:02:54.588
You show up to my house unannounced. what do you think's gonna happen?

887
01:02:54.746 --> 01:02:55.694
Wait. this is your house?

888
01:02:55.781 --> 01:02:57.128
-No. no. Don't. don't. don't.
-Who the hell is that?

889
01:02:57.319 --> 01:02:58.259
Who the hell are you?

890
01:02:58.965 --> 01:02:59.965
She's...

891
01:03:01.269 --> 01:03:02.163
You know.

892
01:03:02.200 --> 01:03:04.059
No. I don't know.
That's why I just asked you.

893
01:03:04.300 --> 01:03:06.831
She's in danger. Frank.
Look. I need your help. okay?

894
01:03:07.093 --> 01:03:09.015
-Yeah. looks like it.
-Well. come on. You owe me.

895
01:03:09.748 --> 01:03:12.045
-For... Aren't you sick of this story?
-Staten Island!

896
01:03:12.200 --> 01:03:13.552
Nah. Staten Island.

897
01:03:13.800 --> 01:03:16.093
What more do you want me to do?
I literally saved your life.

898
01:03:16.279 --> 01:03:17.233
You're out of your mind. kid!

899
01:03:17.312 --> 01:03:18.239
What. I gotta save it twice...

900
01:03:18.418 --> 01:03:19.705
-to get a favor out of you?
-That guy couldn't hit me...

901
01:03:19.825 --> 01:03:21.775
-with a handful of rice.
-I mean. what does that sound like to you?

902
01:03:21.833 --> 01:03:23.375
-I had him exactly where I want him.
-A drug dealer was gonna shoot a guy...

903
01:03:23.400 --> 01:03:24.625
-I'm seein' him right there.
-...then I webbed the gun...

904
01:03:24.650 --> 01:03:25.854
-...out of the drug dealer's hand...
-I know exactly what I'm...

905
01:03:25.879 --> 01:03:27.375
-...completely up for.
-and then kicked that drug dealer...

906
01:03:27.400 --> 01:03:28.282
-Okay. fine. go ahead.
-...back into a storage container.

907
01:03:28.307 --> 01:03:30.014
-What would you call that?
-What does that sound like to you?

908
01:03:31.073 --> 01:03:32.511
I don't care. I just wanna go home.

909
01:03:33.166 --> 01:03:35.183
That's an excellent idea. Kick rocks.

910
01:03:35.310 --> 01:03:37.084
-Go home.
-No. wait. wait. Frank. Frank. Frank. wait.

911
01:03:37.306 --> 01:03:38.271
Please.

912
01:03:39.239 --> 01:03:42.789
I have got to keep her safe. okay?
And I don't have anywhere else to go.

913
01:03:46.929 --> 01:03:48.195
You like chili?

914
01:03:49.273 --> 01:03:50.475
I made chili.

915
01:03:51.800 --> 01:03:52.876
All right. Just...

916
01:03:53.800 --> 01:03:54.975
watch out for the claymores.

917
01:03:55.000 --> 01:03:57.590
Don't wanna pick up pieces of you for the next two weeks.

918
01:03:59.000 --> 01:04:01.238
Hey. I definitely would not eat that chili.

919
01:04:03.000 --> 01:04:04.676
So. you telling me that maniac...

920
01:04:04.756 --> 01:04:08.116
behind all that tank nonsense is nothing but a goddamn teenager?

921
01:04:08.247 --> 01:04:11.868
And it's not just the tank. it's every attack on Damage Control this past month.

922
01:04:12.025 --> 01:04:13.993
And how does a kid learn how to drive a tank?

923
01:04:14.018 --> 01:04:15.168
I don't know. Frank.

924
01:04:15.273 --> 01:04:18.604
-Beat you all over the street like that.
-She did not beat me.

925
01:04:19.233 --> 01:04:20.663
This your family?

926
01:04:23.400 --> 01:04:25.124
Would you get the hell away from that?

927
01:04:25.800 --> 01:04:27.750
Look. I got one rule in this house.

928
01:04:27.926 --> 01:04:30.769
You don't touch anything.
You don't move anything.

929
01:04:30.949 --> 01:04:34.084
You sure as shit don't ask me any goddamn questions about anything.

930
01:04:35.449 --> 01:04:36.856
So. three rules.

931
01:04:39.795 --> 01:04:41.415
I see why you like her.

932
01:04:42.143 --> 01:04:43.876
I'm gonna go put some pants on.

933
01:04:45.107 --> 01:04:46.687
Don't touch the chili.

934
01:04:48.330 --> 01:04:49.677
I like him.

935
01:04:50.420 --> 01:04:51.587
Of course you do.

936
01:04:52.638 --> 01:04:57.018
So I managed to pull this image from my
HUD and run it through the system.

937
01:04:59.556 --> 01:05:00.562
Who is she?

938
01:05:00.587 --> 01:05:03.049
Until a couple months ago. nobody.

939
01:05:03.885 --> 01:05:05.573
She was in and out of foster care.

940
01:05:05.598 --> 01:05:08.865
psych hospitals. and then eventually she
ran away and dropped off the grid.

941
01:05:08.906 --> 01:05:11.052
There's hardly any information about her
that hasn't been scrubbed.

942
01:05:11.077 --> 01:05:14.778
But she's classified as a telepath.
And now we have a name.

943
01:05:18.299 --> 01:05:19.481
Jean Grey.

944
01:05:21.179 --> 01:05:24.795
Yeah. These are the Damage Control sites that she hasn't hit yet...

945
01:05:25.079 --> 01:05:26.407
so if she surfaces...

946
01:05:26.512 --> 01:05:28.654
then my facial tracking program will pick her up.

947
01:05:29.655 --> 01:05:30.655
Right.

948
01:05:30.680 --> 01:05:32.295
Yeah? What then?

949
01:05:34.585 --> 01:05:37.241
Well. don't worry about "what then."
Just look after her.

950
01:05:37.266 --> 01:05:38.702
Don't worry about it?

951
01:05:38.926 --> 01:05:40.692
I'm just supposed to sit here and babysit your girlfriend?

952
01:05:41.000 --> 01:05:42.598
-I don't need to be babysat. so yeah.
-She's not my girlfriend.

953
01:05:42.707 --> 01:05:44.827
All right. all right.
Look. what's the plan?

954
01:05:45.106 --> 01:05:48.488
Just gonna hope that your facial tracking program works?

955
01:05:48.679 --> 01:05:50.885
And you get yourself killed.
I gotta watch her the rest of my life?

956
01:05:51.026 --> 01:05:53.182
I'm not gonna get killed. Frank.
I can catch her. okay?

957
01:05:53.400 --> 01:05:54.275
I just...

958
01:05:54.380 --> 01:05:56.883
I just have to fix my inhibitor and then I'll be good to go.

959
01:05:57.426 --> 01:05:59.040
Well. what do you need to do that?

960
01:06:00.200 --> 01:06:03.890
Frank. You do not have what I need to do that. okay?

961
01:06:05.400 --> 01:06:06.550
You know you've got some mouth on you.

962
01:06:06.712 --> 01:06:08.612
What do you think.
you have an anti-static mat...

963
01:06:08.673 --> 01:06:10.393
a tonal probe. and micro tools?

964
01:06:11.166 --> 01:06:12.761
I got all that shit.

965
01:06:13.359 --> 01:06:14.425
What for?

966
01:06:14.527 --> 01:06:16.077
-Bombs.
-Bingo.

967
01:06:18.200 --> 01:06:19.385
Unbelievable.

968
01:06:31.107 --> 01:06:33.177
Hey. do you think it's safe to maybe call someone...

969
01:06:33.400 --> 01:06:34.970
and let them know I'm okay?

970
01:06:39.506 --> 01:06:40.704
Like your boyfriend?

971
01:06:41.826 --> 01:06:43.943
No. Like my roommate.

972
01:06:48.000 --> 01:06:50.685
I don't think that's such a good idea.
you know. because...

973
01:06:51.547 --> 01:06:54.891
she already knows who he is.
and she can inhabit anyone she wants. so...

974
01:06:55.133 --> 01:06:56.155
Right. Yeah.

975
01:06:56.246 --> 01:06:57.674
Yeah. yeah. yeah. You're right.

976
01:06:57.846 --> 01:07:00.533
-Sorry.
-No. it's fine. I totally get it.

977
01:07:02.433 --> 01:07:03.890
If I called my boyfriend...

978
01:07:04.659 --> 01:07:06.569
he'd just ask me a bunch of questions that I couldn't answer...

979
01:07:06.796 --> 01:07:10.175
and then he'd tell me
I was being withholding again.

980
01:07:10.339 --> 01:07:12.258
-Withholding?
-Yep.

981
01:07:12.399 --> 01:07:14.338
Sounds like your boyfriend's kind of a jerk.

982
01:07:17.112 --> 01:07:18.832
But why'd he think you're withholding?

983
01:07:19.173 --> 01:07:23.109
I don't know. You tell me.
masked vigilante behind the curtain.

984
01:07:25.313 --> 01:07:27.141
Okay. I see your point.

985
01:07:28.953 --> 01:07:30.169
So what about you?

986
01:07:30.600 --> 01:07:31.782
What about me?

987
01:07:32.600 --> 01:07:36.076
Well. do you have a Mrs. Spider-Man?

988
01:07:38.033 --> 01:07:40.379
Do I have a Mrs. Spider-Man?

989
01:07:43.873 --> 01:07:45.695
No. No.

990
01:07:46.573 --> 01:07:47.601
Why not?

991
01:07:47.626 --> 01:07:49.581
Why not? Because I'm...

992
01:07:51.073 --> 01:07:53.091
I'm too withholding. obviously.

993
01:07:54.019 --> 01:07:56.819
Welcome to the club.

994
01:08:02.160 --> 01:08:03.643
There was someone.

995
01:08:04.506 --> 01:08:06.162
-Really?
-Yeah. yeah. yeah.

996
01:08:08.886 --> 01:08:10.011
What happened?

997
01:08:10.633 --> 01:08:11.877
I...

998
01:08:13.400 --> 01:08:14.909
I had to let her go.

999
01:08:16.200 --> 01:08:17.650
To keep her safe.

1000
01:08:21.540 --> 01:08:23.688
I'm sorry.
That must have been really hard for you.

1001
01:08:25.002 --> 01:08:26.950
Yeah. it was. Yeah. It is.

1002
01:08:28.200 --> 01:08:29.432
It is really hard.

1003
01:08:33.453 --> 01:08:34.575
Are you okay?

1004
01:08:34.693 --> 01:08:35.756
Yeah. Yeah. yeah. I'm okay. I...

1005
01:08:35.825 --> 01:08:37.089
You know what. I'm just gonna come over.

1006
01:08:37.173 --> 01:08:39.166
Hold on. hold on. hold on.

1007
01:08:41.166 --> 01:08:42.175
What's going on?

1008
01:08:42.200 --> 01:08:44.033
It just keeps overheating on me.

1009
01:08:44.892 --> 01:08:46.717
It's been stumping me for days.

1010
01:08:47.200 --> 01:08:48.350
Before I switched to aerospace...

1011
01:08:48.375 --> 01:08:52.315
I was gonna major in biochemical engineering.
so. do you mind if I...

1012
01:08:52.503 --> 01:08:53.928
Yeah. for sure.

1013
01:08:53.953 --> 01:08:55.328
Here. There you go.

1014
01:08:59.466 --> 01:09:00.682
Wow.

1015
01:09:03.160 --> 01:09:05.110
So. does the device itself...

1016
01:09:05.262 --> 01:09:08.975
I mean. does it generate any kind of radiation or a magnetic field?

1017
01:09:09.213 --> 01:09:10.512
Cause that would definitely interfere.

1018
01:09:10.600 --> 01:09:14.150
Yeah. it has a micro magnetic field. but I accounted for that in the design.

1019
01:09:14.680 --> 01:09:16.384
Okay. well. what about your suit?

1020
01:09:16.600 --> 01:09:19.941
It actually dissipates into the fabric.
which is pretty cool.

1021
01:09:21.000 --> 01:09:22.102
Okay.

1022
01:09:25.000 --> 01:09:26.321
What about those?

1023
01:09:27.193 --> 01:09:28.554
What about what?

1024
01:09:30.826 --> 01:09:33.519
Your goggles. or whatever you call 'em.

1025
01:09:34.019 --> 01:09:37.431
They would create a field.
It would be tiny. but...

1026
01:09:38.766 --> 01:09:41.267
But it's on your head.
which is very close to the inhibitor.

1027
01:09:41.381 --> 01:09:43.375
Which is probably why it's overheating.

1028
01:09:43.400 --> 01:09:45.331
MJ. that is genius.

1029
01:09:47.153 --> 01:09:48.615
Okay. this has to work.

1030
01:09:52.453 --> 01:09:54.279
Inhibitor engaged.

1031
01:09:55.500 --> 01:09:58.322
Suppressing selected arachnid hormones.

1032
01:09:59.400 --> 01:10:01.191
Okay. That feels better.

1033
01:10:01.446 --> 01:10:02.971
That feels totally better.

1034
01:10:03.332 --> 01:10:05.212
My head feels so clear.

1035
01:10:05.946 --> 01:10:07.198
Web. web.

1036
01:10:07.380 --> 01:10:09.364
And I'm not shooting organic webs.

1037
01:10:09.480 --> 01:10:11.824
My God. MJ. that. like. totally worked.

1038
01:10:12.859 --> 01:10:15.359
You know. this is some really intense stuff you're working on here.

1039
01:10:18.200 --> 01:10:20.012
Well. yeah. it's really important.

1040
01:10:22.340 --> 01:10:26.241
Yeah. but this is like. I mean.
this is like altering your DNA.

1041
01:10:27.207 --> 01:10:30.884
I mean. this is the kind of stuff you put on.
like. I don't know. like a monster.

1042
01:10:32.913 --> 01:10:35.847
Well. if you've seen what's been happening to me over the last couple days...

1043
01:10:36.200 --> 01:10:37.727
then you might understand.

1044
01:10:38.091 --> 01:10:39.541
Yeah. well. I've been with you for the last few hours...

1045
01:10:39.566 --> 01:10:40.812
and that's not what I've seen.

1046
01:10:41.559 --> 01:10:42.874
And what have you seen?

1047
01:10:43.972 --> 01:10:45.407
From my side of the curtain?

1048
01:10:47.159 --> 01:10:50.610
A really good guy who might just be changing.

1049
01:10:56.066 --> 01:10:59.516
Well. I don't mean to overstep.
I'll let you get back to it.

1050
01:11:20.826 --> 01:11:22.413
Can't sleep either?

1051
01:11:22.812 --> 01:11:24.077
You want coffee?

1052
01:11:24.726 --> 01:11:25.899
Sure.

1053
01:11:27.000 --> 01:11:28.401
